From c17b38c36b265638e98f3646d7c56dd44e74d75f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 15:40:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: name the buffers a bounded host split places, and
 refute the read-cost order

The B7c bounded host split says how many bytes it moved to the host-visible
mapping and never which buffers, so nothing in the estate could tell whether
those bytes are read once per token or once per prompt. plan_begin now receives
each buffer's first byte-contributing tensor name, the split receipt names what
it placed, and GGML_VK_ALLOC_TRACE dumps the whole plan.

The commission was an ordering policy - place the cheapest-to-read weight there
first, token_embd being gathered one row per token. That lever does not exist:
token_embd.weight is never in a Vulkan plan at any -ngl, because the loader pins
dev_input to the CPU. The 1.19 GB non-layer tensor in the device batch is
output.weight, read in full for every token's logits and so no cheaper to
displace than the layer weights already chosen. The policy was built, run,
measured byte-identical to plan order, and removed.

Names are advisory: reserve_plan() never reads them, so placement is
byte-for-byte what B7c decided. API version 3 -> 4 (layout unchanged, signature
changed, so an old DSO must be refused rather than miscalled).

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-240 R51 host-split spill order, Opus 5 MEDIUM maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED by the maker - identity and receipts only, no placement change, bit-identical (27B S-X8 generated text sha 04312f94162fc4d31633 across all arms); no t/s predicted, the ordering lever was refuted
Lane: lane-240
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-buffers.cpp; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_630.py)
